WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Governments all over
the world pay producers.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.190
Farmers get paid for crops.

3
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.950
Bus companies get paid to keep fares down.

4
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.630
Often the payment is a fixed
amount for every unit made.

5
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.430
That is a subsidy.

6
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.260
The money goes to the firm.

7
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.680
So does the firm keep all of it?

8
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.580
Or does some reach
shoppers as a lower price?

9
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.800
When a government pays firms
for every item they make,

10
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.530
who ends up with the money?

11
00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:29.170
In this mission, you'll shift
supply down by the subsidy

12
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.900
and find the rectangle
the government pays for.

13
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.630
Then you'll predict what
happens in a graph lab,

14
00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:36.530
and move a slider to check.

15
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: find out who
ends up with the money.
